# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.
#
# The Kokish relay (Bridge Bum, "Kokish Relay"): after 2♣–2♦, opener's
# 2♥ shows either hearts (five or more, unbalanced) or the balanced hand
# that would have rebid 3NT (24-25 on our ladder, strong-openings.bid).
# Responder must bid 2♠, and opener says which:
#
#   2NT  24-25 balanced (game forcing, below 3NT)
#   3♣/3♦/3♠  five or more hearts and four or more of that suit
#   3♥   six or more hearts, one-suited
#
# A balanced hand with five hearts rebids 2NT (22-23) or goes through the
# relay (24-25). See kokish.notes.md.

module kokish "Kokish relay after 2♣–2♦"
  card   two_level.two_clubs.kokish
  needs  strong-openings
  skill  bidding_conventions/kokish

# ── Opener's 2♥: the relay ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Priority 1: it replaces the natural 2♥ and the 3NT rebid of
# strong-openings.bid for the hands it takes.
after 2C (P) 2D (P)
  2H  "Kokish: hearts, or 24-25 balanced"   alert
      shows (H>=5, !balanced) | (balanced, hcp=24..25)
      sets  ask=kokish
      artificial
      priority 1

# ── Responder completes the relay ────────────────────────────────────
when asked kokish
  2S  "Completes the relay (forced)"   alert
      artificial
      priority 2

# ── Opener says which ────────────────────────────────────────────────
when answered kokish
  2N  "24-25 balanced"                        shows balanced, hcp=24..25
      priority 1
  3H  "Six or more hearts, one-suited"        shows H>=6, S<=3, D<=3, C<=3
      priority 1
  3C  "Five or more hearts, four or more clubs"     shows H>=5, C>=4
      priority 1
  3D  "Five or more hearts, four or more diamonds"  shows H>=5, D>=4
      priority 1
  3S  "Five or more hearts, four or more spades"    shows H>=5, S>=4
      priority 1

# ── Responder after the two-suiter: support hearts, raise the second
# suit, or 3NT. Game forcing (the 2♣ opening), so a cheap raise leaves
# room for the slam modules.
after 2C (P) 2D (P) 2H (P) 2S (P) 3x (P) when x is not H
  3H  "Three or more hearts: agrees hearts"   shows H>=3
      sets  trump=H
      priority 1
  4x  "Four or more {x}: agrees {x}"          shows x>=4, H<=2
      when  x is S
      sets  trump=x
      priority 1
  4x  "Four or more {x}: agrees {x}"          shows x>=4, H<=2
      when  x is C | x is D
      sets  trump=x
  3N  "No fit: notrump"                        shows H<=2
after 2C (P) 2D (P) 2H (P) 2S (P) 3H (P)
  4H  "Two or more hearts: game in hearts"     shows H>=2
      sets  trump=H
  3N  "A singleton or void in hearts"          shows H<=1
